# Web Applications (Static & SPA)

**Intent:** Ship, test, and host marketing or product web apps and **host vendored client bundles** (e.g. games). Cross-surface UI policy lives in `universal-product.mdc` §2a. Game engines and replay logic live in `games-building.mdc`.

## Docs map **[core]**

| Doc | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `README.md` | Dev commands, deploy targets, design philosophy |
| `design_spec.md` / `roadmap.md` | Product direction, paused features (e.g. monetization flags) |
| `wrangler.jsonc` / `vercel.json` | Host-specific routing (only the file for your target) |

Read before large changes.

## Stack-agnostic defaults **[core]**

- Prefer **static-first**: content as JSON or markdown under `public/`; minimal server logic.
- Document routing (hash-based or path-based) in README so agents do not guess.
- Global styling: one source of truth (`style.css` or design tokens); if using Tailwind, decide whether preflight is on or off and stay consistent.
- **Monetization:** use explicit feature flags or a documented “monetization paused” constant — do not half-enable paywalls without updating `roadmap.md`.

## UI expectations (web-specific) **[core]**

Apply `universal-product.mdc` §1b (Dieter Rams) on every visual change:

- **As little design as possible:** one type family (or paired set), limited weights, consistent spacing scale; no extra borders, gradients, or shadows unless they encode state.
- **Understandable:** visible labels on primary actions; heading hierarchy (`h1` → `h2`) matches outline order; link text describes destination.
- **Honest:** buttons disabled only when action is unavailable; loading states on async actions; no placeholder “coming soon” that looks clickable.
- **Unobtrusive:** navigation supports reading flow; sidebars and sticky chrome do not cover main CTAs on mobile.
- **Long-lasting:** prefer design tokens / CSS variables in `style.css` over scattered magic numbers; document token meanings in `design_spec.md`.
- Calm typography; edge-to-edge readability; semantic breakpoints (`sm:`, `lg:`); touch-friendly targets; preserve `:focus-visible` — full a11y in `universal-product.mdc` §2a.

## SPA resilience & SEO **[core]**

- **Error boundaries:** route- or section-level fallback UI with retry/home — never a blank screen on render failure.
- **Code splitting:** lazy-load heavy routes (games, admin, charts) via dynamic `import()` or framework equivalent.
- **SEO (per route):** unique `<title>`, meta description, canonical URL, Open Graph tags — even for hash routes, set document title on navigation.
- **`[applicable if TypeScript]`** enable `strict`; prefer `unknown` over `any`; explicit return types on exported functions.

## SPA hosting **[core]**

- Production build outputs to `dist/` (or equivalent).
- **Cloudflare Workers / static assets:** `assets.directory` → `./dist`, `not_found_handling: single-page-application` so unknown paths fall back to `index.html`.
- **Vercel / Netlify:** equivalent SPA rewrite rules in host config.
- **Dev server:** if you vend a nested client SPA under `public/<app>/`, mirror SPA fallback in Vite (or host) preview so deep links work locally — not only in production.

## Hosting vendored sub-apps **[core]**

When embedding a separate client build (games, tools):

1. Upstream build sets correct **asset `base`** subpath.
2. Copy artifacts to `public/<app-id>/` with `index.html` at folder root.
3. Host SPA fallback for `/public-path/*` client routes (host config + dev middleware).
4. Optional theme overlay CSS on parent chrome for contrast when iframe'd.
5. For game-specific iframe height, embed detection, and engine rules → `games-building.mdc`.

## Verification gate **[core]**

Before claiming done:

```bash
npm test
npm run build
npm run test:e2e   # when present
```

- Structural/data tests under `tests/` when applicable.
- **E2E smoke:** extend route list when adding hash or path pages; assert **stable copy** on each route.
- Put **`data-testid`** (or accessible role + name) on anything E2E asserts; cap new spec files at ~3–5 scenarios; reset state in `beforeEach`.
- **Network mocking:** use `page.route` (Playwright) or `cy.intercept` (Cypress) for flaky third parties so CI stays deterministic.
- After changing vendored assets under `public/`, run full build so `dist/` matches.

## Git & deploy **[core]**

- Canonical branch `main`; mirror `master` only if your team still depends on it (`git push origin main:master`).
- After deploy, if users see stale shells: purge CDN cache for `/` and `/assets/*`, hard-refresh; confirm latest CI deploy succeeded.

## What this rule does not cover

- System architecture documents → `system-design.mdc`
- Browser job-application bots → `automation-software.mdc`
- Game simulation, determinism, PWA inside the game → `games-building.mdc`
